#import "template.typ": policy-rule, policy-warning

= General Policy & Compliance

== Purpose and Scope

The purpose of this Corporate Travel and Expense Reimbursement Policy is to establish clear, fair, and consistent standards for business expenditures across all entities and departments of Apex Global Technologies Inc. This policy ensures responsible stewardship of company resources while facilitating efficient business operations.

#policy-rule("POL-GEN-001", "Applicability & Scope")[
  This policy applies uniformly to all full-time and part-time employees, contractors, consultants, and directors incurring business expenses on behalf of the company. Compliance is mandatory regardless of funding source or reporting line.
]

== Employee Fiduciary Responsibilities

Employees traveling or incurring business expenses are expected to exercise good judgment, prudence, and ethical discretion. Business travel should be planned thoughtfully to achieve company objectives at the lowest reasonable cost.

#policy-rule("POL-GEN-002", "Fiduciary Duty & Fair Dealing")[
  Employees must treat company funds with the same care and prudence as their own personal funds. Falsification of expense claims, intentional inflation of amounts, or claiming personal expenditures as business-related constitutes grounds for disciplinary action up to and including termination for cause.
]

== Compliance and Audit Rights

The Global Finance & Internal Audit teams periodically audit expense reports on a random and targeted basis.

#policy-rule("POL-GEN-003", "Audit and Clawback")[
  The company reserves the right to audit any expense report submitted within the preceding twenty-four (24) months. If an improper, unsupported, or fraudulent reimbursement is identified, the company retains the legal right to claw back the funds via payroll deduction or direct invoicing.
]
